 ## Background
-The Asymptotic Decider was introduced by Nielson and Hamann in the paper "The Asymptotic Decider: Resolving Ambiguities in Marching Cubes" [S1][S2, unofficial]. It was developed to address the issue of topological ambiguities in Marching Squares, which can lead to incorrect surface reconstructions. The method has since been widely adopted in 2D isosurface extraction algorithms [S2, unofficial].
